  "name": "Question 8",
  "problem": "$\\,$ $x=3$\n\nThe predicate $P(x)$ is given above. Which of following represents $\u00acP(x)?$",
  "worked_solution": "In plain English, our predicate $P(x)$ means the following:\n\n$\\,$ $x$ equals $3.$\n\nThe symbol \"$\u00ac$\" represents negation. To negate our plain English expression, we place the words \"It is not true that\" in front of it. This gives the following:\n\n$\\,$ It is not true that $x$ equals $3.$\n\nIn other words, $x$ is *not equal to* $3.$ Therefore, $\u00acP(x)$ means the following:\n\n$\\,$ $x\\ne 3$",
